<section class="white" id="onboarding">
  <div class="wrap case-grid">

    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Employee Experience &amp; Retention
      </p>

      <h2>Redesigning the First 90 Days</h2>

      <p>
        At a residential youth services program,
        one home was experiencing exceptionally high
        turnover among new direct care employees.
        Approximately 90% were leaving within
        their first 90 days.
      </p>

      <p>
        Rather than treating turnover solely as an
        employee performance issue, I looked at how
        we prepared and supported people entering
        a demanding work environment.
      </p>

      <p>
        I redesigned the onboarding process to include
        completed training before placement, experienced
        peer mentors, a gradual transition to independent
        work, and structured conversations with leadership.
        We also addressed staffing coverage and training
        accountability.
      </p>

      <p>
        The process required coordination across
        residential homes and created additional
        opportunities for employees to share concerns
        before those concerns led to resignations.
      </p>

      <ul class="key-points">
        <li>
          60 hours of training completed before
          the first floor shift
        </li>
        <li>
          A structured 30, 60, and 90 day
          onboarding progression
        </li>
        <li>
          Volunteer mentorship and leadership
          check ins
        </li>
      </ul>

      <a class="button"
         href="Onboarding_Case_Study.pdf"
         target="_blank"
         rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Read the Full Case Study
      </a>
    </div>

    <aside class="stat-card">
      <div class="stat">90% → 30%</div>

      <p class="stat-label">
        Approximate first 90 day turnover at
        the highest turnover home, before and
        after implementation.
      </p>

      <div class="stat-divider"></div>

      <div class="stat">9 months</div>

      <p class="stat-label">
        Approximate length of time the program
        operated during my tenure.
      </p>

      <p class="fine-print">
