      <p class="eyebrow">
        Business Process Automation &amp; Compliance
      </p>

      <h2>
        Policy Lifecycle Management
        &amp; Workflow Automation
      </h2>

      <p>
        Managing hundreds of organizational policies
        required significant administrative coordination.
        Review deadlines, document requests, approvals,
        and publication records were tracked through
        largely manual processes.
      </p>

      <p>
        I developed a connected workflow using Excel,
        Microsoft Power Automate, Outlook, OneDrive,
        and SharePoint to automate routine administrative
        steps and improve visibility into the process.
      </p>

      <p>
        The system initiated review requests, captured
        returned documents, updated tracking information,
        and notified appropriate staff when approved
        policies were ready for publication.
      </p>

      <p>
        An important part of the design was recognizing
        what should remain a human responsibility.
        Compliance review, evaluation of operational
        practices, and board approval were intentionally
        kept outside the automated process.
      </p>

      <ul class="key-points">
        <li>
          Automated review scheduling and
          document routing
        </li>
        <li>
          Integrated tracking across Microsoft 365
          applications
        </li>
        <li>
          Human approval checkpoints and
          workflow failure alerts
        </li>
      </ul>

      <a class="button"
         href="Policy_Automation_Portfolio.pdf"
         target="_blank"
